__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv*/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
runs/
# AppWorld's task data, downloaded by `appworld download data` (see README). ~90MB and not ours to
# vendor; it lives here rather than in the JAZ checkout so no path leaves this repo.
/data/
# The other half of `root: .`: AppWorld WRITES `experiments/` (per-task working databases) into the
# root it is given, so a run drops one here. Ignored for the same reason as `data/`, and because
# `provenance.json` lists untracked files individually -- unignored, every run would grow it by one
# entry per working DB.
/experiments/
*.log

# Secrets. These hold real OpenAI keys and are read at launch (scripts/run_appworld_official_react.sh
# treats .env as authoritative), so they must never be committable -- the pattern covers variants like
# .env2 and .env.local as well. Ignored rather than tracked-with-placeholders on purpose: a tracked
# .env invites someone to fill it in and commit the fill.
.env
.env*
